    "summary": "High‑energy first set classics and a blazing Dark Star jam sequence",
    "blurb": "The show delivers tight, inspired versions of Jack Straw, Brown Eyed Women and El Paso, while the second set erupts into a soaring Dark Star > Me & My Uncle > Dark Star > Sitting On Top Of The World suite. Vocal performances on Comes A Time and Truckin' are standout, and the overall playing is consistently high‑octane.",
    "review": "December 5, 1971 at New York's Felt Forum captures the Dead in a rare moment of pure, unfiltered vigor. The first set rolls out classic material—Bertha, Brown Eyed Women, Jack Straw, El Paso—with Jerry’s phrasing shimmering and Bob’s vocals cutting through with palpable excitement. The real highlight arrives in the second set: a Dark Star jam that morphs into Me & My Uncle, returns to Dark Star and lands on Sitting On Top Of The World, showcasing Keith’s bright piano voicings and Bill’s steady drive behind the rhythm section. Truckin' and Comes A Time close the night with soulful storytelling from Phil and a soaring vocal finish on Johnny B. Goode, making this Felt Forum performance one of the most electrifying snapshots of the early‑’70 era.",
